{
  "_comment": "Weapon-type mechanics and named items for Fortune's Weave: 6 weapon types and 29 named objects, of which 8 name a dungeon recorded on the locations page.",
  "_mechanics": {
    "noTriangle": "The weapon triangle is not part of this game. Each weapon type instead carries its own baseline mechanic, which is what the weapon type table records.",
    "cursedObjects": "Cursed objects are a special item type in Dagda, appearing as weapons and as accessories, and possession is what appears to grant access to Blaze Arts.",
    "gaugeInteraction": "Using a cursed weapon adds to the Blaze Art gauge of units with Underworld Blaze Arts, while units with Celestial Blaze Arts have their gauge depleted instead, and the gauge of Orchel is unaffected either way.",
    "diadem": "Using a cursed weapon or equipping a cursed accessory gives a chance to activate the Diadem of Duality. Cai and Theodora, whose cursed objects are embedded in their bodies, hold it inherently regardless of what they carry.",
    "drakes": "Several cursed objects are called Drake's treasures after the pirate Drake, who was their original owner, and collectors such as Talimun hunt them down.",
    "combatArts": "Named weapons are what unlock Combat Arts, for example Full Moon on Mahadu's Spear.",
    "scope": "The weapon and spell table is recorded separately on the weapons page; this page records the weapon-type mechanics and the named cursed objects with their wielders and acquisition sources."
  },
